Collate the president's review notes, without acting on them
Bryan sent two annotated PDFs on 4 September — `Home Page.pdf` and
`Reserve Page.pdf`, printed from the staged site with his comments in red.
This puts them in the repository where we work, instead of in an inbox.

**No site copy changes here.** That is the point of the PR. You said you have
to digest this before it is authoritative, so nothing he suggested has been
applied — not the tagline, not the intro rewrite, not the equipment paragraph.
The new file records what was said and where each note would land if you say
yes.

## What's in it

- **`REVIEW-NOTES.md`** — new. Round 1 is Bryan's two PDFs, quoted close to
  verbatim, organised by page. Structured to take more rounds as they arrive
  (you mentioned more emails), newest at the bottom.
- **`_config.yml`** — excludes it from the Jekyll build. Non-front-matter `.md`
  files get copied verbatim to a public URL otherwise; the file's own comment
  says MANIFEST, REDIRECTS and RESERVE-DESIGN all leaked that way once. This
  one is unratified board feedback plus a list of what we think is unresolved,
  so it is the worst candidate for that.
- **`CONTENT-TODO.md`** — five pointers, on the items his notes actually touch.
  CONTENT-TODO stays the list of what is needed; nothing moved out of it.

## The five things that are genuinely yours to call

Everything else is a copy edit. These change what the site claims:

1. **Credit card: a hold, or a card on file?** The page says "a temporary
   charge as collateral." His paragraph says "a valid credit card for late fees
   and incidentals." Different arrangements, and the second is the one members
   ask about.
2. **Equipment Terms and Conditions** — his copy names the document by title.
   It does not exist. The copy can't ship ahead of the document.
3. **Where do events come from?** He wants a calendar of classes, meetups and
   outside video events (Comic Con). Classes are in `_data/classes.yml`;
   meetups and video events have no source anywhere. That is the work — the
   rendering is an afternoon.
4. **Is equipment checkout self-serve or staff-picked?** His intro rewrite
   says "check out production equipment"; the rest of the site says members
   describe the job and staff pull the gear.
5. **Video or slideshow** in the slot the floor plan would vacate. Different
   builds.

## Two things worth acting on regardless

**He offered to shoot the photography.** *"I can take and send you the
pictures."* That is the dependency under the hero photo, a picture per
facility, and the slideshow — three things that have been waiting on it. Worth
taking him up on before the layout work, because how that section is designed
depends on what the pictures look like.

**There is a dated change: 1 November 2026.** `equipment@fcpublicmedia.org` is
live in M365; he switches equipment requests to it on that date and announces
it in the October newsletter. Until then `fcpmequipment@gmail.com` stands. It
is one line in `_data/org.yml` and it is exactly the kind of thing that gets
sailed past — TODO: it probably wants a real reminder, or an advocate seat,
rather than a sentence in a notes file. I did not build one; say the word.

## Verified

`_config.yml` parses and `REVIEW-NOTES.md` is in `exclude` — checked with
Ruby's YAML loader. I could **not** run a Jekyll build to confirm the file
stays out of `_site/`: `bundle exec jekyll` reports the gem is missing in this
worktree. The exclude entry is textually identical in form to the six around
it, so the risk is low, but it is asserted rather than observed.

## Deliberately not done

- No page copy touched.
- No `image:` key added to `_data/facilities.yml` — that waits on photographs.
- No advocate seat for the November date.
- His mission statement is quoted, not installed in `_data/org.yml`.
